{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"agent-skills","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Agent skills"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A model's training data does not contain Kirana, so a coding agent left to itself\nwrites Tailwind or StyleX and calls it Kirana. The "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/project/llms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"plain-text docs"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nexplain the system; the two skills in Kirana's repository tell an agent how to\nwork in it: what to check first, which mistakes compile and still render wrong,\nand what to run when something does."}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"npx skills add kirana-style/kirana                 # both\nnpx skills add kirana-style/kirana --skill kirana  # one","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> skills add kirana-style/kirana                 <span class=\"th-token th-comment\"># both</span>\n<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> skills add kirana-style/kirana <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">--skill</span> kirana  <span class=\"th-token th-comment\"># one</span>","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"skills","source":"skills"}}]},{"type":"text","value":" command installs them for\nthe agent you use (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, OpenCode and the others it\nsupports), in your project or globally with "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"-g","source":"-g"}},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> skills update","source":"npx skills update"}},{"type":"text","value":" keeps\nthem current."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"They live in the repository's "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"skills/","source":"skills/"}},{"type":"text","value":" folder; to try a change to them before it\nis merged, point the command at a checkout ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> skills add ./kirana","source":"npx skills add ./kirana"}},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-each-one-teaches","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What each one teaches"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skill"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the agent loads it"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What it carries"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana</span>","source":"kirana"}}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the project imports "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"@kirana-style/core","source":"@kirana-style/core"}},{"type":"text","value":", or a style compiles and renders wrong"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the rules that cause real bugs, the loop below, where each new thing goes, and the habits to unlearn"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"kirana-migrate","source":"kirana-migrate"}}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"asked to port components or an app from Tailwind, shadcn/ui or StyleX"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the codemods and their reports, the traps in both directions, and how to prove the port renders the same"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each skill is short (the rules and the workflow), and keeps the detail in\nreference files the agent reads only when it needs them: the API, how "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":" is\nspelled in each framework, the Tailwind and StyleX mappings, and two files\ngenerated from the compiler's source on every build: every\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tooling/diagnostics","children":[{"type":"text","value":"diagnostic"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with what to do about it, and every\n"},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tooling/lint","children":[{"type":"text","value":"lint rule"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with the linters that run it. A diagnostic added\nto the compiler without a line saying what to do about it fails the build."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-loop-it-follows","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The loop it follows"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Learn the project."}]},{"type":"text","value":" Run "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tooling/cli#kirana-style-export","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">export</span>","source":"kirana-style export"}}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nfor the tokens, themes, recipes and relations that exist, by their real names,\nthen "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> doctor","source":"kirana-style doctor"}},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Write the style"}]},{"type":"text","value":", with the rules: conditions inside the value, entries\nmerge per condition, "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":" forwarded last, "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"styleProps","source":"styleProps"}},{"type":"text","value":" for installed\ncomponents, colours as "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">light-dark</span>()","source":"light-dark()"}},{"type":"text","value":" pairs."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> check","source":"kirana-style check"}}]},{"type":"text","value":", and fix every error by its code."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lint"}]},{"type":"text","value":", with whichever of Oxlint, ESLint or Biome the project runs."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> trace file:line property","source":"kirana-style trace file:line property"}}]},{"type":"text","value":" when it compiles and looks wrong."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">kirana-style</span> doctor <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">--report</span>","source":"kirana-style doctor --report"}}]},{"type":"text","value":" when it looks like a Kirana bug, and ask before\nfiling it."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every step answers from the compiler, so an agent that follows it checks its own\nwork instead of guessing whether a class string it remembered still exists."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"with-llms-txt","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With llms.txt"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The skills and the "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/project/llms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"plain-text docs"}]},{"type":"text","value":" do different jobs. A\nskill is instructions an agent loads by itself when the task matches; "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"llms.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">txt</span>","source":"llms.txt"}},{"type":"text","value":"\nis reference it reads when it needs to know more. The skills link to the\nmarkdown pages instead of copying them, so the two never disagree."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"agent-skills","text":"Agent skills","level":1},{"id":"what-each-one-teaches","text":"What each one teaches","level":2},{"id":"the-loop-it-follows","text":"The loop it follows","level":2},{"id":"with-llms-txt","text":"With llms.txt","level":2}]}
